# Defense-in-depth: never publish internal docs.
# The package.json "files" allowlist is the primary control (explicit per-file
# entries under docs/). This .npmignore is a second guard so that if a glob is
# ever re-introduced, these internal doc patterns still get excluded.

docs/*-plan.md
docs/*-compliance.md
docs/security-audit-report.md
docs/research-synthesis*.md
docs/mega-*.md
docs/chrome-brain-*.md

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tests must never ship in the published package. The auditoria-pos-190 found
# ~36 test files leaking into the tarball via the `.sinapse-ai/**` and
# `packages/installer/tests/**` allowlist entries. These add weight and expose
# internal test scaffolding with zero runtime value.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/__tests__/**
**/tests/**
**/*.test.js
**/*.spec.js

# EXCEPTION: scaffold templates under development/templates/ intentionally ship
# example tests so generated projects/squads start with a test harness. These
# are template payloads, NOT tests run against this package — keep them.
# (`index.test.ts.hbs` is a Handlebars template, not a runnable .test.js; the
#  squad-template example test is copied verbatim into new squads.)
!.sinapse-ai/development/templates/**

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Nested node_modules — NEVER ship. The `.sinapse-ai/` allowlist entry in
# package.json `files` was dragging `.sinapse-ai/node_modules/**` (~6.9k files,
# ~21 MB) into the tarball. Every runtime dep `.sinapse-ai/**` needs is declared
# in the ROOT package.json `dependencies`, so they resolve from the consumer's
# node_modules — the nested copy is a local dev artifact only.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/node_modules/**

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build artifacts & archives — NEVER ship. The Vite-built health dashboard was
# dragging its `dist/` (a ~595 kB bundle + a ~2.5 MB `.js.map` sourcemap) into
# the tarball, plus two doc `.zip` archives — ~3.2 MB of dead weight with ZERO
# runtime value (nothing serves `health-dashboard/dist`; the live `graph`
# dashboard is a different module). These are non-reproducible build outputs and
# archives; the dashboard SOURCE (`health-dashboard/src/**`) still ships so the
# bundle can always be rebuilt. Drop the built output, keep the source.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/dist/**
**/*.map
**/*.zip
